REWRITTEN FOR BUILD 42

Build 41 script and Lua conventions did not survive the move to build 42, so the
following were rebuilt rather than carried over. Each was verified against a
local build 42 install before being changed.

  Craftable appliances
    The originals were "item ... Type = Moveable" plus "recipe Make ...".
    Build 42 ships 969 craftRecipe blocks and no legacy recipe blocks at all, so
    both appliances were unbuildable. They are now entity definitions with
    SpriteConfig and CraftRecipe components, following the pattern the base game
    uses for its own craftable furniture. Ingredients, skill gates and XP awards
    were carried across unchanged.

  Item declarations
    "Type = Normal" and "Type = Moveable" became "ItemType = base:normal" and
    "ItemType = base:moveable". The moveable concept still exists; only the key
    changed.

  Recipe callbacks
    The Recipe.OnCreate and Recipe.OnGiveXP namespaces no longer exist in build
    42, so the server Lua that defined handlers against them raised on load and
    took the rest of the mod's server code with it. XP is now declared directly
    on each recipe with xpAward, and the file was removed.

  Guitar dismantling
    Build 42 consolidated the six coloured electric guitar variants into
    GuitarElectric and GuitarElectricBass. The recipe referenced item ids that no
    longer resolve.

  Component salvage
    A misspelled item id, Base.ElectronicScrap, silently produced nothing. The
    correct id is Base.ElectronicsScrap.

  Translations
    Build 42 reads translations as JSON. The mod's Tooltip_EN.txt was never
    loaded, so its tooltip did not appear. Replaced with Tooltip.json.

  Tile geometry
    Build 42's renderer needs per-tile geometry for custom tilesheets; without
    it, appliances render flat or disappear behind walls. tileGeometry.txt was
    written for this project. The box heights in it are estimated from the sprite
    art and want a visual pass in game.


